def abstract():
    mark_with("fm:abs", Paragraph("ABSTRACT", FRONTH))
    sp(4)
    p("Customer churn — the discontinuation of a service by an existing customer — is "
      "a recurring problem for subscription-based businesses, where retaining an "
      "existing customer is generally less expensive than acquiring a new one. "
      "Conventional reporting tools describe churn only after it has occurred and "
      "offer little guidance on which individual customers require attention. This "
      "project addresses that gap by developing <b>ChurnIQ</b>, an end-to-end customer "
      "churn prediction and business intelligence system that converts raw customer "
      "data into customer-level risk intelligence and prioritised retention actions.")
    p(f"ChurnIQ is implemented in Python and organised into eleven source modules "
      f"under a <font face='Courier' size='10'>Src/</font> package, together with a "
      f"Streamlit application (<font face='Courier' size='10'>app.py</font>) that "
      f"serves as the user interface. The system implements a complete data-science "
      f"workflow: dataset validation for CSV, XLS and XLSX uploads; data cleaning; "
      f"exploratory data analysis; a scikit-learn preprocessing pipeline combining "
      f"median imputation and standard scaling for numerical attributes with "
      f"most-frequent imputation and one-hot encoding for categorical attributes; "
      f"supervised model training; model evaluation; churn prediction; customer risk "
      f"scoring and segmentation; and rule-based retention recommendations.")
    p(f"Six classification algorithms — Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random "
      f"Forest, Extra Trees, Gradient Boosting and Histogram-based Gradient Boosting — "
      f"were trained and compared on the IBM Telco Customer Churn dataset "
      f"({N_ROWS:,} customer records, {N_COLS} attributes, churn rate "
      f"{CHURN_RATE:.2f}%). Using an 80:20 stratified train–test split with a fixed "
      f"random state, the training module ranks models by F1 score and persists the "
      f"selected pipeline. The saved model is <b>Random Forest</b>, which achieved an "
      f"accuracy of {pct(RF['Accuracy'])}, recall of {pct(RF['Recall'])}, F1 score of "
      f"{pct(RF['F1 Score'])} and ROC-AUC of {pct(RF['ROC-AUC'])} on the held-out test "
      f"set. Gradient Boosting recorded the highest accuracy ({pct(GB['Accuracy'])}) "
      f"and ROC-AUC ({pct(GB['ROC-AUC'])}) but substantially lower recall "
      f"({pct(GB['Recall'])}), and the trade-off between these two selection criteria "
      f"is analysed in the report.")
    p(f"The prediction layer applies a three-tier strategy so that datasets other than "
      f"the reference dataset can also be analysed: the saved model is used when the "
      f"uploaded data is compatible, an adaptive model is trained when a churn label "
      f"is present but the schema differs, and a heuristic behavioural risk engine is "
      f"used when no label is available. Predicted probabilities are converted into a "
      f"0–100 risk score, four risk levels and six strategic customer segments, which "
      f"are then mapped to retention priorities and engagement channels. On the "
      f"reference dataset the pipeline classified {PIPE['critical']:,} customers as "
      f"Critical and {PIPE['high']:,} as High risk, and estimated the associated "
      f"revenue exposure.")
    p("Results are presented through an eleven-page Streamlit dashboard supporting "
      "dataset upload, data-quality inspection, churn analytics, prediction, risk "
      "analysis, segmentation, customer-level exploration, model comparison, "
      "recommendations and CSV report downloads. The project demonstrates how a "
      "predictive model can be embedded within an interactive analytical application "
      "so that statistical output is translated into information that supports "
      "retention decision-making.")
    sp(8)
    p("<b>Keywords:</b> Customer churn prediction, machine learning, classification, "
      "scikit-learn, customer segmentation, risk scoring, business intelligence, "
      "Streamlit dashboard, exploratory data analysis, retention analytics.")
    story.append(PageBreak())


