def chapter15():
    h1("CHAPTER 15<br/>CONCLUSION")
    p("This project set out to design and implement a system that predicts customer "
      "churn and converts those predictions into information that can support "
      "retention decisions. The objective has been met. ChurnIQ is a working "
      "application that accepts a customer dataset, validates and cleans it, analyses "
      "it, predicts churn for every customer, scores and segments the customer base, "
      "generates retention recommendations, and presents the results through an "
      "interactive dashboard with exportable reports.")
    p(f"The technical work is grounded in the data. Exploratory analysis of the IBM "
      f"Telco Customer Churn dataset ({N_ROWS:,} records, {N_COLS} attributes, "
      f"{CHURN_RATE:.2f}% churn) established that contract type, payment method and "
      f"tenure are the attributes most strongly associated with churn: month-to-month "
      f"customers churn at 42.71% against 2.83% for two-year contracts, "
      f"electronic-check payers at 45.29% against 15.24% for automatic credit-card "
      f"payment, and customers in their first six months at 52.94% against 6.61% beyond "
      f"sixty months. These findings shaped the risk-scoring weights and the "
      f"recommendation rules, so the analytical layer and the business layer rest on "
      f"the same evidence.")
    p(f"Six classification algorithms were trained under identical conditions and "
      f"compared on five metrics with stratified cross-validation. Random Forest was "
      f"selected on the basis of the highest F1 score ({pct(RF['F1 Score'])}) and the "
      f"highest cross-validated F1 mean ({RF['CV F1 Mean']:.4f}), achieving accuracy "
      f"{pct(RF['Accuracy'])}, recall {pct(RF['Recall'])} and ROC-AUC "
      f"{pct(RF['ROC-AUC'])} on the held-out test set. The selection criterion was "
      f"deliberately chosen: F1 rather than accuracy, because on an imbalanced target a "
      f"model can appear accurate while detecting few churners. The trained pipeline is "
      f"persisted together with its preprocessing and metadata, allowing it to be "
      f"reused and its applicability to new data to be checked automatically.")
    p(f"The intelligence layer converts probabilities into decisions. Applied to the "
      f"reference dataset it classified {PIPE['critical']:,} customers as Critical and "
      f"{PIPE['high']:,} as High risk, distributed the customer base across six "
      f"strategic segments, and estimated the associated revenue exposure. The analysis "
      f"showed that the 260 customers in the High Value At Risk segment carry greater "
      f"aggregate exposure than the 963 in Critical Retention — a conclusion available "
      f"only because risk and value are considered together, and one that would change "
      f"how a retention budget is allocated.")
    p("Beyond the modelling, the project required a number of engineering decisions "
      "whose importance became apparent only during implementation: fitting the "
      "preprocessor exclusively on training data to prevent leakage; storing "
      "preprocessing and estimator in a single pipeline so that training and inference "
      "cannot diverge; recording the feature list in the model metadata so that "
      "compatibility can be verified before use; configuring the encoder to tolerate "
      "unseen categories; guarding every optional import so that one missing component "
      "cannot disable the application; and reporting which prediction method produced "
      "each result so that a heuristic estimate is never mistaken for a model "
      "prediction.")
    p("The system has limitations, which are stated in Chapter 14 rather than "
      "understated. It was trained on a single dataset; it does not identify every "
      "churner; hyper-parameters were set manually; it cannot explain individual "
      "predictions; and it lacks authentication, automated retraining and deployment. "
      "Two internal inconsistencies were also identified through the analysis performed "
      "for this report — the divergence between the F1-based and ROC-AUC-based "
      "definitions of the best model, and the two different sets of risk-level "
      "thresholds. Both are documented, and correcting them is straightforward.")
    p("The principal outcome of the project is the demonstration that the distance "
      "between a trained classifier and a usable business tool is itself substantial "
      "engineering work. A probability of 0.83 is not an insight; a ranked worklist of "
      "customers with risk levels, segments, estimated revenue exposure and a suggested "
      "engagement channel is. ChurnIQ implements that translation end to end, and in "
      "doing so provides practical experience of the complete data-science lifecycle — "
      "from raw data through analysis and modelling to an application that presents "
      "results in terms a business user can act upon.")
    story.append(PageBreak())


